
---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Recipe Guides | Silken Valley Lifestyle"
  heroTitle="Recipe Guides"
  heroText="Cooking knowledge, ingredient references, kitchen techniques, and inspiration for everyday meals."
  heroCompact={true}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Art of Cooking</p>
    <h1>Recipe Knowledge & Kitchen Reference Library</h1>
    <p>
      Discover helpful cooking guides, ingredient information,
      preparation techniques, and culinary inspiration.
      From everyday meals to traditional recipes and special
      occasions, explore the knowledge that makes cooking
      more enjoyable and rewarding.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid">
    <a class="card" href="#cooking-basics">
      <h3>Cooking Basics</h3>
      <p>Essential cooking methods, kitchen terminology, and foundational techniques.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#ingredients">
      <h3>Ingredient Guides</h3>
      <p>Understanding ingredients, substitutions, storage, and flavour combinations.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#measurements">
      <h3>Measurements & Conversions</h3>
      <p>Kitchen measurements, temperature conversions, and recipe scaling.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#baking">
      <h3>Baking & Pastry</h3>
      <p>Flour, leavening agents, baking techniques, pastry, and desserts.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#herbs">
      <h3>Herbs & Spices</h3>
      <p>Flavour profiles, seasoning techniques, and culinary herb combinations.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#vegetables">
      <h3>Vegetables & Fruits</h3>
      <p>Preparation, cooking methods, seasonal produce, and storage advice.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#meat">
      <h3>Meat, Poultry & Seafood</h3>
      <p>Preparation methods, cooking temperatures, and safe food handling.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#meal-planning">
      <h3>Meal Planning</h3>
      <p>Organizing weekly meals, preparing ingredients, and reducing food waste.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#preserving">
      <h3>Food Preservation</h3>
      <p>Freezing, drying, refrigeration, and safe preserving principles.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#world-cuisine">
      <h3>World Cuisine</h3>
      <p>Traditional cooking styles, regional ingredients, and international flavours.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#sauces">
      <h3>Sauces, Stocks & Dressings</h3>
      <p>Foundational sauces, flavourful stocks, marinades, and salad dressings.</p>
    </a>

    <a class="card" href="#entertaining">
      <h3>Entertaining & Special Occasions</h3>
      <p>Menu planning, presentation, seasonal celebrations, and hosting ideas.</p>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="cooking-basics">
    <p class="eyebrow">01 · Essential Techniques</p>
    <h2>Cooking Basics</h2>
    <p>
      Develop confidence in the kitchen by understanding
      fundamental cooking techniques. Explore boiling,
      simmering, steaming, roasting, grilling, sautéing,
      braising, and frying.
    </p>
    <p>
      Learn how heat affects ingredients, how to prepare
      equipment, and how to build flavour through proper
      preparation and cooking methods.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="ingredients">
    <p class="eyebrow">02 · Understanding Food</p>
    <h2>Ingredient Guides</h2>
    <p>
      Discover the characteristics and uses of everyday
      ingredients, including grains, legumes, dairy products,
      oils, sweeteners, and specialty foods.
    </p>
    <p>
      Explore suitable substitutions, ingredient storage,
      freshness, and how different ingredients work together
      to create balanced flavours and textures.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="measurements">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 · Kitchen Reference</p>
    <h2>Measurements & Conversions</h2>
    <p>
      Understand common kitchen measurements and how to
      convert between metric and imperial quantities.
      Explore volume, weight, oven temperatures, and
      practical recipe scaling.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="baking">
    <p class="eyebrow">04 · The Science of Baking</p>
    <h2>Baking & Pastry</h2>
    <p>
      Explore the fundamentals of baking, including flour
      varieties, yeast, baking powder, baking soda, fats,
      sugars, and eggs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Learn about mixing methods, dough preparation,
      pastry techniques, oven temperatures, and the
      importance of accurate measurements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="herbs">
    <p class="eyebrow">05 · Flavour & Seasoning</p>
    <h2>Herbs & Spices</h2>
    <p>
      Discover the aromas and flavour profiles of culinary
      herbs and spices. Explore classic combinations,
      seasoning methods, dried versus fresh herbs,
      and how to build depth in savoury dishes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="vegetables">
    <p class="eyebrow">06 · Fresh Produce</p>
    <h2>Vegetables & Fruits</h2>
    <p>
      Learn how to select, prepare, store, and cook
      seasonal fruits and vegetables. Explore roasting,
      steaming, blanching, grilling, and other methods
      that bring out natural flavours.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="meat">
    <p class="eyebrow">07 · Preparation & Cooking</p>
    <h2>Meat, Poultry & Seafood</h2>
    <p>
      Understand different cuts, preparation techniques,
      marinades, and cooking methods. Learn the importance
      of food safety, avoiding cross-contamination, and
      using a food thermometer to check safe internal
      cooking temperatures.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="meal-planning">
    <p class="eyebrow">08 · Everyday Organization</p>
    <h2>Meal Planning</h2>
    <p>
      Make everyday cooking more manageable through
      thoughtful meal planning, organized shopping lists,
      ingredient preparation, and efficient use of
      leftovers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Explore ways to plan balanced menus, save time,
      and make the most of ingredients already in your kitchen.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="preserving">
    <p class="eyebrow">09 · Storing & Preserving</p>
    <h2>Food Preservation</h2>
    <p>
      Learn the principles of refrigeration, freezing,
      drying, and preserving. Understand safe storage
      practices, food freshness, and the importance
      of following tested preservation methods.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="world-cuisine">
    <p class="eyebrow">10 · Culinary Traditions</p>
    <h2>World Cuisine</h2>
    <p>
      Explore the ingredients, techniques, and culinary
      traditions of different regions. Discover how
      local produce, cultural influences, and traditional
      methods shape distinctive cuisines around the world.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="sauces">
    <p class="eyebrow">11 · Building Flavour</p>
    <h2>Sauces, Stocks & Dressings</h2>
    <p>
      Discover the foundations of flavourful cooking
      through stocks, broths, sauces, marinades,
      vinaigrettes, and dressings.
    </p>
    <p>
      Learn how to balance acidity, richness, seasoning,
      and texture to complement different dishes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero" id="entertaining">
    <p class="eyebrow">12 · Hospitality & Presentation</p>
    <h2>Entertaining & Special Occasions</h2>
    <p>
      Plan memorable meals and gatherings with practical
      guidance on menu selection, preparation schedules,
      table presentation, seasonal dishes, and hosting.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Continue Exploring</p>
    <h2>More Recipes & Cooking Inspiration</h2>
    <p>
      Visit our Recipes section for delicious dishes,
      cooking ideas, and inspiration for your kitchen.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/recipes/">Explore Recipes →</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/resources/">← Return to Resources</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
